          "name": "t:names.content",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>At Penya Collective, luxury is rooted in integrity. Radiance should not come at a cost to people or planet. Below is how we practise what we believe.</p><h3>Small-Batch Production</h3><p>We produce in intentionally limited quantities. This reduces excess stock, minimises waste, and ensures every piece receives the attention it deserves from the hands that make it.</p><h3>Materials with Meaning</h3><p>We prioritise premium, long-lasting natural fibres — including hemp, organic cotton, and responsibly sourced blends. These materials are chosen not just for their feel, but for their lower environmental footprint and durability over time.</p><h3>Fair Wages &amp; Artisan Partnership</h3><p>We collaborate directly with skilled Zimbabwean artisans and makers, ensuring fair compensation and transparent working conditions. Our supply chain is built on relationship, not extraction.</p><h3>Timeless Over Trend</h3><p>Fast fashion relies on obsolescence. We design for permanence — silhouettes and craftsmanship that remain relevant across seasons. The most sustainable garment is the one you keep wearing.</p><h3>Continual Improvement</h3><p>We are transparent about where we are still growing. We are actively working to improve supply chain documentation, expand our use of certified materials, and reduce our shipping footprint. We welcome accountability from our community.</p>",
